    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a fair point. but if you look at most urban studies, they usually say that density is actually better for the environment and economy in the long run. so when you're looking at these criticisms, do you see them as legitimate long-term obstacles, or are they just short-term growing pains that cities eventually solve?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
