      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "From an urban planning perspective, while density offers long-term environmental and economic benefits, the perceived obstacles are often real short-term friction points. Traffic and utility strains are legitimate capacity issues that can paralyze a project if infrastructure doesn't scale with the build-out. Successfully navigating these criticisms requires developers to proactively fund and integrate necessary public improvements, turning \"growing pains\" into demonstrable community benefits.",
      "source": "target",
